Cevell Platform Licensing Overview

The Cevell Confidential Computing platform is organized into two distinct licensing tiers:

- Core First-Party Platform Software: Governs Cevell software (including `cevell-node`, `cevell-initrd`, orchestration scripts, and build expressions) under the PolyForm Shield License 1.0.0 set forth below, accompanied by the explicit scope clarifications.
- Third-Party Components: Upstream software packages and modules bundled or aggregated within the bootable CVM disk images (e.g., Linux kernel, NVIDIA open kernel modules, Busybox, Go standard runtime) are governed by their respective upstream licenses detailed in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

================================================================================
EXPLICIT PERMITTED & PROHIBITED USE SPECIFICATION
================================================================================

This specification outlines the permitted and prohibited uses under the PolyForm Shield License 1.0.0 for all first-party Cevell software:

1. PERMITTED USES (Internal Commercial Self-Hosting & Evaluation Allowed):
   - Internal Commercial & Business Operations: Deploying, configuring, and running self-hosted instances on private hardware, on-premises data centers, or private cloud environments for internal operations, proprietary applications, and confidential data processing, provided that the deployment is NOT offered as a competing product or service to third parties.
   - Academic & Personal Research: Using, studying, and modifying the software for academic research, personal curiosity, algorithmic experimentation, and public knowledge sharing.
   - Experiments & Benchmarking: Benchmarking throughput, latency, cryptographic overhead, and hardware enclave performance in non-competing test environments.
   - Security Audits & Vulnerability Research: Conducting source code audits, formal verification, fuzz testing, static/dynamic security analysis, and penetration testing.
   - Cryptographic & Silicon Attestation Verification: Inspecting and compiling the source code to independently audit and reproduce binary hashes (dm-verity root hashes, UKI PCR values, MRTD/RTMR measurements) to verify genuine hardware silicon attestation reports (Intel TDX, AMD SEV-SNP, NVIDIA Confidential Computing).
   - Non-Commercial & Educational Organizations: Deployment and use by registered charities, educational institutions, public research laboratories, public health/safety entities, and government agencies.

2. PROHIBITED USES (Competing Products & Commercial Arbitrage Strictly Prohibited):
   - Hosted Services & Cloud Platforms: Providing the software, its runtime, or its functionality as a hosted service, managed service, cloud platform, compute-as-a-service, or API platform to third parties that competes with Cevell or cevell.com.
   - Commercial Arbitrage & Reselling: Selling, sublicensing, leasing, renting, or reselling access to the software or derived images, or offering turnkey confidential VM deployments as a paid infrastructure service to third parties.
   - Competing Products & Substitutes: Developing, distributing, or marketing any product or service that serves as a practical commercial substitute for the Cevell platform or services offered by Cevell.
   - Commercial Inquiries: Any use to provide hosted services, managed cloud infrastructure, or competing commercial offerings requires a separate commercial partnership agreement from Cevell. For commercial inquiries, please contact: contact@mail.cevell.com or visit https://cevell.com.

3. DISTRIBUTION CONDITIONS & OBLIGATIONS:
   - Preservation of Notices: Any distribution of the software, whether modified or unmodified, must include this complete LICENSE file, a reference to https://polyformproject.org/licenses/shield/1.0.0, and the Required Notice specified below.
   - Reciprocal Shield Scope: Any derivative works or changes must be distributed strictly under the same PolyForm Shield License 1.0.0 terms. You may not impose additional restrictions or sublicense the software under different terms.
   - Free of Licensing Fees: You may not charge licensing fees, royalty fees, or access fees for the software or its derivatives.
   - Patent Defense: Any legal action asserting patent infringement against the licensor regarding this software immediately revokes all patent licenses granted hereunder.
   - Cure Period: Unintentional non-compliance can be cured within 32 days of receipt of written notice, after which licenses permanently terminate if not remedied.

